                <pb facs="0409" n="316" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3231/1015: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-09-12T18:00:00-03:00">September 12, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>222. My 219, September 9, 6 p.m.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d337-f1"/> Trade agreement
                    approved by Chamber this afternoon by vote of 127 to 51.</p>
                <p>The agreement will now go to Senate for approval after which it must return to
                    Chamber for signature of the Chairman.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
